{
  "KL_vs_entropy_route_audit": {
    "Jensen_warning": "ConvexOn.map_integral_le requires integrability of f and g∘f and convex continuous closed-domain conditions. Scalar Jensen of xlogx alone is not the functional marginal-entropy contraction needed by tensorization.",
    "chain_rule": "InformationTheory.klDiv_compProd_eq_add is genuine ENNReal chain rule for finite measures/Markov kernels, including infinite branches. To express our F product density and conditionals would require actual normalized conditional kernels on zero fibers, RN/log identities and finite-L1 bridges. This is a valid alternative larger analytic task, not a public certificate or direct ready producer.",
    "data_processing": "InformationTheory.klDiv_map_le gives each marginal KL<=joint KL separately; it does not imply their sum<=joint KL. Two DPI applications are not tensorization.",
    "totalized_warning": "RNLogRatio.toReal_klDiv_eq_integral_logRatio_of_probability has absolute continuity but does not produce finite KL or L1. ENNReal.toReal(infinity)=0 and nonintegrable real Bochner integrals totalize; do not infer finiteness from this equality. Real integral_add/sub/Fubini and KL.toReal entropy identification require separately established actual domains."
  },
  "actor": "phase_source_reviewer_20261005",
  "artifact_kind": "bounded-continuous-product-entropy-source-dependency-preread",
  "authored_route_at_most_seven_steps": [
    "1. For bounded measurable nonnegative F on probability product, derive actual joint/slice/marginal measurability and L1 of F, Phi(F), A,B,Phi(A),Phi(B), and conditional entropy. Phi is continuous on [0,C]; use bounded domination and genuine product/slice Fubini.",
    "2. Set delta_n=1/(n+1), F_n=F+delta_n. Then A_n=A+delta_n, B_n=B+delta_n, m_n=m+delta_n, and every quantity is positive bounded for each fixed n. No positive mass or positive fiber premise is added to F.",
    "3. Define actual R_n(x,y)=A_n(x)*B_n(y)/m_n, positive bounded above/below for fixed n, with integral R_n=m_n. Fixed-n logs/products are genuinely integrable.",
    "4. Integrate u*log(u/v)-u+v>=0 with u=F_n,v=R_n, derived from Real.self_sub_one_le_mul_log(u/v). Expand real logs and use Fubini to obtain integralPhi(F_n)+Phi(m_n)-integralPhi(A_n)-integralPhi(B_n)>=0. The inequality is proved inside, never supplied.",
    "5. Let delta_n->0 using actual bounded xlogx DCT and scalar continuity. Pass only Phi(F_n),Phi(A_n),Phi(B_n),Phi(m_n). Do not pass cross-log terms near zero. This includes F zero on positive sets and m=0.",
    "6. Establish the actual entropy-chain identity using the already produced L1 before subtraction; rewrite marginal inequality as binary product entropy subadditivity and derive marginal entropy contraction by cancellation of finite conditional term.",
    "7. Iterate over finite independent coordinates with actual product/coordinate-replacement adapters and marginal entropy contraction. This iteration is a separate assembled producer until proved; applying scalar C2 compact LSI uses actual coordinate slices, never assumes RMS marginal sqrt functions remain C2."
  ],
  "created_utc": "2026-10-07T06:28:17.079339+00:00",
