    "For actual32 C2 sqrt-density f, chi_R f is compactC2. Existing radial cutoff0<=chi<=1, smoothness/support/gradientO(1/R)/pointwise1 primitives are present. Entropy domination can use |qlogq|+q/e because (chi^2 q)log(chi^2 q)=chi^2 qlogq+q chi^2 log(chi^2); both terms genuinely L1. Gradient error uses fL2 and gradfL2, not additional norm(x)*f moments.",
    "Assemble actual mass/entropy/energy cutoff limits; this remains missing, not implied by existing cutoff API. Source32 produces required domains internally; source33 coherent same-law finite canonicalKL then identifies entropy and energy1/4 to yield KL<=I/2.",
