  "hypothetical_binary_leaf_seven_slots": {
    "conclusion": "Ent_(mu.prod nu)(F) <= integral_y Ent_mu(F(.,y))dnu + integral_x Ent_nu(F(x,.))dmu, with every entropy and outer integral genuinely integrable. Equivalent marginal inequality: integral Phi(A)dmu + integral Phi(B)dnu <= integral Phi(F)d(mu.prod nu)+Phi(m). Marginal entropy contraction and finite-product iteration are subsequent exact consequences requiring chain/Fubini adapters.",
    "constants": "No entropy loss constant; Gaussian scalar LSI retains coefficient2. Phi(0)=0, n0 product law entropy0, finite-Hilbert0 included later. Pi coordinate energy is sum_i partial_i^2, not the default product-max norm squared.",
    "domains": "Arbitrary measurable spaces, real-valued bounded nonnegative functions; no topology, dimension, smoothness or positive lower bound needed. The intended compact C2 squared-function consumer derives C from compact support/continuity and does not expose C as a source premise.",
    "hypotheses": "Actual probability laws, measurable F, 0<=F<=C for a real C>=0. These are generic function-class assumptions. For F=g^2, signed g and arbitrary zeros are permitted; C2/compact support belongs to the eventual consumer. No normalized F, mass positivity, inequality bound, Jensen certificate or moment assumption.",
    "objects": "Probability measures mu on measurable X and nu on measurable Y; measurable F:X×Y->Real, 0<=F<=C. Phi(t)=t*log(t), Phi(0)=0. A(x)=integral F(x,y)dnu, B(y)=integral F(x,y)dmu, m=integral F d(mu.prod nu).",
    "quantifiers": "For each pair of probability laws and each actual measurable bounded nonnegative F, derive joint, all slice, marginal and expected-conditional L1 domains before the inequality. No pre-supplied marginal entropy or conditional-law certificate. This is mathematical proposal syntax, not a typechecked seal.",
    "scope": "Authored sufficient analytic background for compact Gaussian tensorization, not a standalone printed SPHMC theorem, not Bernoulli induction and not a supplied entropy inequality premise. Restricted bounded class rather than the larger unbounded SLT public contract. Zero mass m=0 is included; underlying laws are probabilities, not arbitrary zero measures."
